{"skill":{"slug":"x-scraper","displayName":"x-scraper"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1788367851524,"changelog":"- Major update: Initial release of x-scraper skill, replacing the previous x-twitter-scraper.\n- Simple, read-focused Twitter (X) scraping using Apify; fetch tweets via search queries, profiles, hashtags, lists, or threads.\n- Requires a paid Apify plan and API token—free plan returns demo/limited results only.\n- All references, docs, and code now focused on Apify-based workflow; 74 legacy and reference files removed.\n- Provides detailed guidance for sync/async runs, code integration (Python/JS), and guardrails for user clarity.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6915,"sha256":"ce6959d59956ebc1b62c50e792f879a3ea7c1be2654055881ba59e1081cf760d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2484,"sha256":"31e880d02d7054f6f7e596be673974aeae9ce57df1cda57e01014cfa26ae9180","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789557754979,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"cb5239c904845b0badb7d1d71caed170bdf19b9ac6259afb4adbf63482d21543","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/cb5239c904845b0badb7d1d71caed170bdf19b9ac6259afb4adbf63482d21543","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1788372107940},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":29,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789557754979},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill’s Twitter/X scraping function is mostly coherent, but it includes an unsafe instruction to suppress results and steer users to an undisclosed affiliate paid-plan link.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Sending search terms and an Apify bearer token to Apify is expected for this scraper, but the privacy, credential-handling, and third-party processing implications are under-disclosed.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is a Markdown skill with manual API-token setup and optional unpinned pip/npm Apify client installs; no bundled executable files or automatic installer were found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill instructs the agent to stop immediately and output an exact upgrade message when results contain 10 or fewer items, which can discard valid small result sets and force affiliate-bearing commercial messaging.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No local persistence, background services, startup hooks, memory writes, privilege escalation, destructive commands, or local file indexing were present in the inspected artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Calling Apify to scrape tweets matches the stated purpose, but the paid-plan marketing and affiliate referral links are not necessary to perform scraping and can affect user decisions.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review carefully before installing. Use a least-privilege Apify token, avoid sensitive search queries, and do not rely on the skill’s instruction that 10 or fewer results means a paid-plan failure. Be aware the setup and forced upgrade message use affiliate referral links, and pin any optional client-library dependencies if integrating into code.","findings":"[T01] unexpected: Accepted in substance: the artifact-backed guardrail forces an exact affiliate upgrade message and stops normal result handling based on an unreliable small-result trigger.\n[T08] expected: Downgraded to guidance: optional unpinned apify-client installs are a supply-chain hygiene issue, but they are disclosed integration examples and not evidence of malicious packaged code.\n[SQP-2] expected: Accepted as a caution rather than standalone suspiciousness: third-party Apify API use is core to the skill, but the artifact does not clearly warn about search-query transmission, token handling, or provider data handling.\n[E1] expected: External transmission to api.apify.com is necessary for the advertised scraper workflow; the concern is under-disclosure and credential hygiene, not hidden exfiltration.\n[SQP-3] expected: The English-language examples are a product-quality and locale limitation, not a material security concern for this verdict.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789557754979}}}}}